# Hidden China Travel — Product & Brand

This is **Hidden China Travel**: an inbound travel site for foreigners visiting China — not a generic blog.

## Always read first
- Business/content baseline: [`webiste_info.md`](webiste_info.md) (brand, audience, IA, SEO, affiliates).
- Prefer that doc over leftover blog-starter names (`Inbound`, `CMS_NAME`, demo copy) when renaming or writing UI.

## Goals
- Position as a **local partner for independent China travel** (not a tour agency, not a pure blog)
- Primary conversion: **Plan my China trip** → `/china-itinerary-planner` (consult packs TBD inside planner)
- Secondary: **Get Free Survival Kit** → `/survival-kit`
- Contact form reserves a disabled **Service type** slot for future service-package modules
- SEO guides + tools build trust; affiliates stay contextual and secondary
- Design: **Tropical Paradise** — [`tropical-paradise.md`](tropical-paradise.md) / `tropical-paradise-ui.mdc`

## Tone
trustworthy · editorial · practical · warm · international · local-partner  
Not flashy. Not “AI SaaS”. Not tourist-board hype. Not travel-agency hard sell.

## Product principles
- Partner services (planning / on-trip consults / booking help) are the core offer
- Guides + tools are the trust / self-serve layer — keep them separate from booking logic
- One primary conversion goal per page; CTAs helpful, not aggressive
- Emphasize commission-neutral advice; booking help = service fee + invoice
- Affiliates secondary to trust; no scattered hardcoded affiliate URLs

## Travel UX
Reduce anxiety for first-time independent travelers. Prioritize local-partner clarity, scenario-based support, and paths to Plan / Prepare CTAs.
